# Text is stored and checked out with \n, on Windows too. Listing the types by hand is what let
# .css, .json, .scm, .props, .snap and .slnx through, and carriage returns fail `format --check`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# What is not text. The .gz are the compiled grammars, the only binaries actually in here.
*.gz binary
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ai binary
*.psd binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
